151
00:10:31,274 --> 00:10:35,777
Models, AI models, just to make make sure.

152
00:10:36,715 --> 00:10:39,827
we're on the right track. AI models don't read text,

153
00:10:39,827 --> 00:10:46,432
they read numbers. A tokenizer is a translator that converts your prompt

154
00:10:46,653 --> 00:10:51,396
into a sequence of numbers the model actually can process.

155
00:10:51,396 --> 00:10:56,139
So models read numbers. Rule of thumb:

156
00:10:56,139 --> 00:10:57,701
you don't have to remember this one,

157
00:10:57,701 --> 00:11:03,595
but it's interesting. One token equals 0.75.

158
00:11:04,223 --> 00:11:06,754
English words or about four characters.

159
00:11:06,754 --> 00:11:12,117
An example of that is let's say you have the prompt a brutalist concrete pavilion

160
00:11:12,117 --> 00:11:15,659
at sunset. That is what we as humans prompt,

161
00:11:15,659 --> 00:11:18,661
but that's not what the model actually reads.

162
00:11:18,661 --> 00:11:20,882
The model would read something like this:

163
00:11:20,882 --> 00:11:24,684
clip, it's just the name of a tokenizer,

164
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:26,605
translates this sentence.

165
00:11:29,887 --> 00:11:34,099
into "a", "brutal"... sorry, "a", "brutal",

166
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:38,442
ist concrete pavilion at sunset

167
00:11:38,802 --> 00:11:43,855
and for every token so brutal is

168
00:11:43,855 --> 00:11:48,227
a token ist is a token it gives

169
00:11:48,468 --> 00:11:54,621
one number right so this sequence of numbers is just

170
00:11:54,621 --> 00:11:57,052
how the computer reads this

171
00:11:59,201 --> 00:12:04,064
This sentence. Just something to think about whenever you see tokens.

172
00:12:04,064 --> 00:12:10,547
Tokens is a translation from words to later numbers.

